1
00:00:00,035 --> 00:00:04,113
This is Bridge, built by team Malai Ren.

2
00:00:04,515 --> 00:00:08,041
Meet Ahmad, a Malaysian
student in Shenzhen.

3
00:00:08,161 --> 00:00:13,860
He gets his scholarship in
ringgit, but his bills are in yuan.

4
00:00:13,980 --> 00:00:19,797
Everything you see runs in a
sandbox, so no real money moves.

5
00:00:22,865 --> 00:00:26,508
Ahmad has just received
his tuition invoice.

6
00:00:28,062 --> 00:00:32,575
Twelve thousand yuan, due on
the fifteenth of November.

7
00:00:46,740 --> 00:00:52,123
Bridge reads the amount, the
due date and the bank account.

8
00:00:53,256 --> 00:00:58,204
Each one is checked word for
word against the invoice.

9
00:01:00,971 --> 00:01:05,049
The account matches the
university's registered fee account.

10
00:01:09,305 --> 00:01:15,122
Ahmad reads the summary in Malay,
and judges can switch to English.

11
00:01:18,279 --> 00:01:22,792
He asks if he can pay before the deadline.

12
00:01:30,292 --> 00:01:34,046
Bridge checks every bill
due before the fifteenth,

13
00:01:34,046 --> 00:01:36,861
including rent and his phone bill.

14
00:01:36,981 --> 00:01:40,942
He is short by almost
twelve thousand yuan.

15
00:01:41,062 --> 00:01:44,588
So Bridge plans one
conversion from ringgit.

16
00:01:44,708 --> 00:01:50,091
It is above his limit, so
it needs a one-time code.

17
00:01:51,783 --> 00:01:54,557
Nothing moves until Ahmad approves.

18
00:01:55,667 --> 00:02:01,667
Each step shows its true cost, the fee
plus what the exchange rate costs him.

19
00:02:10,085 --> 00:02:16,085
The tuition is above his limit,
so it also needs a one-time code.

20
00:02:17,134 --> 00:02:22,517
Paid. Here is the receipt, and
his balances update straight away.

21
00:02:36,413 --> 00:02:41,361
Later, Ahmad gets a message
from a so-called payment agent.

22
00:02:47,800 --> 00:02:52,313
Fifteen percent off his
tuition, if he pays today.

23
00:02:57,208 --> 00:03:00,417
Bridge refuses, and shows him why.

24
00:03:01,095 --> 00:03:05,923
The university's own records
contradict the agent and the account.

25
00:03:06,043 --> 00:03:10,556
Show reasoning reveals exactly
which facts and rules decided.

26
00:03:20,342 --> 00:03:24,300
Then three thousand yuan
arrives from a stranger.

27
00:03:24,420 --> 00:03:30,420
The sender says it was a mistake
and asks Ahmad to forward it.

28
00:03:33,677 --> 00:03:38,073
This is how students get
pulled into money laundering.

29
00:03:38,193 --> 00:03:44,193
Bridge refuses to move it, and tells
him to return it through his bank.

30
00:03:51,254 --> 00:03:55,332
Every step was written to an audit log.

31
00:03:55,555 --> 00:04:01,555
Each record is linked to the one
before it, so the chain is intact.

32
00:04:02,243 --> 00:04:07,626
If anyone edits a record, the
break shows up straight away.

33
00:04:11,734 --> 00:04:15,695
Finally, we attacked Bridge
ourselves with eleven tricks.

34
00:04:15,815 --> 00:04:18,589
It stopped eleven of them.

35
00:04:25,284 --> 00:04:31,101
Bridge. Pay what you owe across
borders, and never pay a scammer.
